1
00:00:00,170 --> 00:00:04,025
My Diwali leave… on hold? And
Rohan's… approved?

2
00:00:04,025 --> 00:00:07,733
Ten minutes later, same dates.
Manager favouritism.

3
00:00:07,733 --> 00:00:11,227
Riya starts typing: 'No
problem, I'll cancel.'

4
00:00:11,227 --> 00:00:15,186
Wait. In the Mahabharata, Ekalavya
did the same thing.

5
00:00:15,186 --> 00:00:17,286
Drona refused to teach him.

6
00:00:17,286 --> 00:00:20,413
He made a clay image of
Drona, and taught himself.

7
00:00:20,413 --> 00:00:22,920
So good that even
Arjuna fell behind.

8
00:00:22,920 --> 00:00:25,026
And Arjuna? Drona's favourite.

9
00:00:25,026 --> 00:00:26,487
Just like Rohan.

10
00:00:26,487 --> 00:00:30,058
Drona asked for his teacher's fee…
his right thumb.

11
00:00:30,058 --> 00:00:32,408
'Without a second thought…

12
00:00:32,408 --> 00:00:35,048
he cut off his thumb and gave it
to Drona.' Avicharya means…

13
00:00:35,048 --> 00:00:36,805
without a second thought.

14
00:00:36,805 --> 00:00:40,379
He gave it, smiling. After that,
his arrows slowed.

15
00:00:40,379 --> 00:00:43,724
For us today: don't cut off your
thumb… for someone's favourite.

16
00:00:43,724 --> 00:00:47,867
Riya deletes 'cancel'… and sends:
'One leave roster for everyone?'

17
00:00:48,037 --> 00:00:51,119
What would you do? Cancel quietly…
or ask for the rule?
